      <h2>What Just Happened</h2>
      <p>Nvidia reported the most impressive quarter in its history. Revenue of <strong>$81.6 billion</strong> grew 85% year-over-year and 20% sequentially — crushing the Wall Street consensus of $79.2 billion by $2.4 billion. The company earned <strong>$1.87 per share</strong> (non-GAAP), beating estimates of $1.78. And for Q2, Nvidia guided to <strong>$91 billion in revenue</strong> — $3 to $5 billion above what the street was modeling.</p>
      <p>This wasn't just a beat. This was a statement. The AI infrastructure supercycle is not slowing down — if anything, it's accelerating. And Nvidia, sitting at the center of it all, is compounding at a pace that is almost unprecedented for a company of its size.</p>
    </div>

