      <h2>The Growth That Defies Comprehension</h2>
      <p>Let's put these numbers in perspective. Nvidia's Data Center segment alone — at $75.2 billion — generated more revenue in a single quarter than most Fortune 500 companies generate in an entire year. Data Center Networking grew <strong>199% year-over-year</strong>. That's not a typo — networking revenue nearly tripled in twelve months.</p>
      <p>The company earned <strong>$58.3 billion in GAAP net income</strong> in a single quarter. For context, that's more than Apple earns in most full fiscal years. And unlike many high-growth tech companies, Nvidia is generating this profit while simultaneously investing aggressively in R&D and infrastructure.</p>
